text @[Tomoya]
text Phew...
text I take a break after bringing the stuff to the corner of the garden.
text Leaf mold, fertilizer, flowers, a bag with additional tools and accessories.
text After parting with Kyou and the others yesterday, I spent all of my savings on these things.
text I mixed and matched the different types of flowers I found in the gardening section.
text Even in their plastic pots, their colors are bringing life back to the garden.
text Using a hose, I draw some water from the faucet.
text I scrub down the dirty bricks with the water.
text Then I lay down the leaf mold.
text I mix it with the soil I dug up last night, then till it with a spade. I'll let it sit in the sun for a while.
text Next up is some lawn maintenance.
text I don't have time to lay new sod, so I decide to just mow the existing grass.
text I change out the lawnmower's blades and oil them up.
text Starting at the edge of the lawn, I push the lawnmower with all my strength.
text There's a loud rumbling sound as the tires and blades start to spin.
text A shower of grass kicks up into the air, spewing into a receptacle.
text I don't know how many times I walk back and forth mowing the entire lawn.
