text The garden looks really different now that the grass is trimmed.
text It looked so gloomy up to now, but it suddenly seems much brighter.
text The last thing to work on is the flower bed.
text I take the flowers from their pots and plant them one by one, keeping color coordination in mind.
text The bricks draw a gently sloping curve.
text The blooming flowers of early summer give off fresh fragrances and colors.
text The open space with its clean-cut grass.
text In the middle of it all is a bright white table and two garden chairs.
text I feel a strange sense of confirmation, as if the jigsaw pieces of my dreams are sliding into place.
text I forget everything and immerse myself in gardening.
