music BGM05B.mp3
text The garden is back to how it used to be.
text The precious place where Kotomi and I first met.
text I can't believe that I actually finished it.
text The types of flowers or the length of the grass might not be exactly right.
text But still, I did everything I could.
text I don't think anything's missing.
text Wait, yes there is.
text One large and very important piece is still missing.
text In order for it all to come together...
text All I can do now is wait.
text I just realized that I'm insanely tired.
text It's a comfortable sort of exhaustion. I feel like I could sleep for days.
text But I can't sleep just yet.
text Now that the garden is back to the way it used to be, there are other things to do.
text I go to a garden chair which now looks just like it does in my memories.
text I poke at the seat to make sure the paint is dry.
text And then I slowly sit down.
text I put on my jacket and rummage around in my pockets.
text Inside is the book that Kotomi entrusted to me.
text The book with the leather cover.
text Like some old and worn dictionary, the edges of the pages are curled.
text I open the cover to take a look inside.
text The faded pages have a color similar to baked bread and the book is worm-eaten in many places.
text Why did Kotomi tell me not to read it?
text The answer must be inside.
text @[Tomoya]
text Sorry, but I'm going to read it.
text I whisper that to suppress the small pangs of guilt I'm feeling.
text I turn to the inside cover and start reading.
text It seems like... a collection of short stories.
text Possibly because the book is translated from another language, it's far from an easy read.
text I skim through the first few stories and move on to another one.
text It appears to be a story about a girl who says she's from the future who meets a middle-aged man...
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text Soon, I look up from the pages.
text @[Tomoya]
text *Yawwwwwwn*
text I let out a big yawn.
text I'm extremely sleepy.
text It must be because of how comfortable the garden is.
text I try to return my attention to the book.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text I realize that the book has slipped from my fingers onto my lap.
text The gentle wind flips through the pages.
