text Unable to bear it anymore, I close my eyes.
text A soft sense of sleepiness wraps around my head.
text A distant memory washes over me like a high tide.
text Back then...
text That's right, I was with Kotomi...
text No, that's not true.
text That book was newer, bigger, and had a nicer binding.
text Low tide arrives to sweep me away, and my consciousness fades.
delay 30
sound VYQ.aac
text "Day before yesterday I saw a rabbit..."
text Gradually, I forget where I am and what day it is.
delay 30
sound VYR.aac
text "...and yesterday a deer..."
text I sense that I'm very close to being swept away into sleep.
text That's right.
text It's not that the book was bigger. We were...
text We were smaller.
