text After that, I went to visit her house almost every day.
text Lots of sun from the garden shone on the floor of her living room.
text I could smell the lingering fragrance of a tobacco pipe.
sound E5Q.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text It's the smell of Daddy's tobacco.
text Even as a child, that seemed high class to me. It was different from what the other adults smoked.
text She enjoyed playing house the most.
text But playing house with her was... a little different.
text She pointed at and named each of the dishes with her chubby finger.
text After that, she placed her palms together.
sound E5R.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Let us eat.
text @[Tomoya]
text Let's eat...
sound E5S.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Please help yourself.
text She made a big deal out of it and stared at me.
sound E5T.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Say "ah."
text She picked up the "food" with some disposable chopsticks and held it out in front of me.
text And when I didn't put it in my mouth, she looked like she was about to cry.
text @[Tomoya]
text I can't eat this.
text The feast was made out of clay.
text @[Tomoya]
text No fair. You have to eat it too, Kotomi-chan.
text @[Tomoya]
text Here's your half, Kotomi-chan.
text I put a lot of the clay cooking onto her paper plate.
sound E5U.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Yes. This is my half.
sound E5V.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Halfsies with Tomoya-kun.
text She gave a big smile.
delay 60
text In the end, I never told my other friends about that garden.
text I never really liked playing in large groups anyway...
text I wanted to keep this secret all to myself.
