text When it was nice out, we'd play in the garden.
text We'd run around barefoot on the lawn and play tag or hide-and-seek.
text But there were too few people for tag, and she'd always be on the verge of tears if I found a great hiding spot.
text There were many different kinds of flowers blooming in the small flower bed.
text She knew the names of all of them.
sound E5W.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text This is a California poppy, this is a begonia, this is a pansy...
sound E5X.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text And this one is...
sound E5Y.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Chry...
text @[Tomoya]
text Chry?
sound E5Z.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Um...
sound E60.aac
text @[Mother]
text Chrysanthemum paludosum.
sound E61.aac
text @[Mother]
text It's also called a North Pole.
text Her mother, who was in the garden hanging up the laundry, gently taught us.
text She was wearing her usual bright white apron.
text She was always smiling.
text I was envious.
text This is what I wanted most in the world.
sound E62.aac
text @[Mother]
text Say, Kotomi-chan. Since the weather's so nice, why don't you go play outside with Tomoya-kun?
text Kotomi always looked troubled whenever she was told to do that.
sound E63.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text But we're already outside.
sound E64.aac
text @[Mother]
text This is just our garden, isn't it?
sound E65.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text The garden is outside.
sound E66.aac
text @[Mother]
text But...
sound E67.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text It's outside.
text She wouldn't budge.
text Her mother sighed and looked into Kotomi's face.
sound E68.aac
text @[Mother]
text "Outside" means beyond the hedge.
sound E69.aac
text @[Mother]
text The outside world is very big and has lots of stuff you've never seen before, Kotomi-chan.
sound E6A.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text It's scary, so I don't want to.
text @[Tomoya]
text It's not scary at all.
text I said that as someone who came from "outside."
sound E6B.aac
text @[Mother]
text That's right...
sound E6C.aac
text @[Mother]
text Tomoya-kun is a really good boy.
sound E6D.aac
text @[Mother]
text Kotomi-chan is a bad girl.
sound E6E.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I'm not a bad girl.
sound E6F.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I want to go outside, but...
sound E6G.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I'll do it next time.
text After she said that, her mother burst out laughing.
text I didn't understand what was so funny.
sound E6H.aac
text @[Mother]
text ...Well, let's have snack time.
text She brought us a freshly-baked sponge cake and some mysterious tea that smelled like flowers.
sound E6I.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text My mommy made this.
sound E6J.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text It's very good.
sound E6K.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Let us eat.
text @[Tomoya]
text Let's eat...
text After repeating after her, I picked at a slice in the middle.
sound E6L.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Tomoya-kun, um...
sound E6M.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text The ones on the end taste best.
text She said that with more confidence than when she recited the flower names.
