delay 60
text On cold days, we read together.
text I knew right away that she was different from the other kids.
text She easily read books with difficult words and kanji characters.
sound E6N.aac
text It's hard to write, but reading is easy.
text Her smile was tinged with pride when she said that.
text Her favorite book was this brand new, really nice looking book with a brown leather cover.
text She said her father bought it for her when she entered elementary school.
text I found it boring because it was too difficult to read.
sound E6O.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text It's not interesting?
text Noticing that I wasn't having any fun, she asked me that while tilting her head to one side.
text @[Tomoya]
text I don't get it.
sound E6P.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text It's the same for me...
sound E6Q.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text But Daddy told me to read lots of books.
text @[Tomoya]
text This is too hard.
sound E6R.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text He said that it doesn't matter if I don't understand it yet.
sound E6S.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text He said that I'll understand one day.
sound E6T.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text He said it's because there's lots of stuff I still have to learn.
sound E6U.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text I want to read all of the books in the world.
sound E6V.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text If I can learn lots of stuff, that would be very, very wonderful.
sound E6W.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Don't you think so, Tomoya-kun?
text @[Tomoya]
text Yeah, I guess...
text She smiled at me despite my halfhearted answer.
text She really looked happy.
sound E6X.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Oh, I know. I've got a good idea.
sound E6Y.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text Let's just read the wonderful parts.
sound E6Z.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text We'll read them again and again until we memorize them.
sound E70.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text And then someday we can think of them even without the book.
sound E71.aac
text @[Kotomi]
text So let's start from the beginning.
text She started reading her favorite parts awkwardly.
text I tried to follow along.
text I felt like a terrible student...
text She was diligent and kept trying to teach me again and again...
